{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ותכל כל עבדת משכן", :translit "va-teichel kol avodat mishkan", :gloss "and was finished all the work of the Tabernacle"} {:he "בעשרים וחמשה בכסלו", :translit "be-esrim u-ve-chamesha be-kislev", :gloss "on the twenty-fifth of Kislev"} {:he "נגמר", :translit "nigmar", :gloss "it was completed"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ותכל כל עבדת משכן", :b "בעשרים וחמשה בכסלו"}], :frame {:text "The Tabernacle was completed and erected on the first day of the first month (Exodus 40:2, 40:17). The twenty-fifth of Kislev, nine months and ten days earlier, is when the work of construction was finished. This same date later became the dedication day of the Second Temple (Zechariah 7:1 identifies Kislev by name; Haggai 2:18 speaks of the foundation day on the twenty-fourth of the ninth month, i.e., Kislev). The gematria linking the Tabernacle's completion text to this date binds the original Tabernacle dedication to the future Temple dedication commemorated by Chanukah (Megillat Antiochus; I Maccabees 4:52–59).", :sources ["Exodus 40:2" "Exodus 40:17" "Zechariah 7:1" "Haggai 2:18" "Megillat Antiochus" "I Maccabees 4:52-59"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ותכל", :translit "va-teichel", :gloss "and was finished"} {:he "כלה מלאכת כל העולם", :translit "kelah melakhat kol ha-olam", :gloss "was finished the work of all the world"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: va-teichel (was finished) read as kelah (completed/bringing to end) applied to all the world's work."}], :frame {:text "The Tabernacle's completion mirrors the completion of Creation: just as Genesis 2:1–2 states 'the heavens and the earth were finished' using the same root כלה, the Tabernacle constitutes the completion of God's purpose for the entire world. Midrash Tanchuma states that the work of Creation was not complete until the Tabernacle was built, reading Exodus 39:32 ('all the work was finished') as a cosmic completion paralleling Genesis 2:1 ('the heavens and the earth and all their array were finished'). Pseudo-Jonathan on Exodus 39:43 renders the blessing over the Tabernacle with the language of Genesis 1:31, tying Tabernacle to Creation.", :sources ["Genesis 2:1" "Genesis 2:2" "Midrash Tanchuma Pekudei 11" "Pseudo-Jonathan Exodus 39:43"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ותכל כל עבדת משכן", :a-value 1392, :b "בעשרים וחמשה בכסלו", :b-value 1099, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: va-teichel (was finished) read as kelah (completed/bringing to end) applied to all the world's work.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:34.580033850Z", :model "glm-5.2"}